\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a complete separable metric space (X,d), integer $n\geq 2$ and $\kappa \in R$, is being an n-dimensional Alexandrov space of curvature $\geq \kappa $ equivalent to full-support $RCD((n-1)\kappa ,n)$ with measure $H^{n}_d$ and distributional curvature satisfying $R(A,B,B,A)(f)\geq \kappa \int f(|A|^{2}|B|^{2}-\langle A,B\rangle ^{2})dH^{n}$ for every nonnegative test function f and test vector fields A,B? Use the unreduced RCD and test classes in the cited theorem.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a complete separable metric space (X,d), integer $n\geq 2$ and $\kappa \in R$, is being an n-dimensional Alexandrov space of curvature $\geq \kappa $ equivalent to full-support $RCD((n-1)\kappa ,n)$ with measure $H^{n}_d$ and distributional curvature satisfying $R(A,B,B,A)(f)\geq \kappa \int f(|A|^{2}|B|^{2}-\langle A,B\rangle ^{2})dH^{n}$ for every nonnegative test function f and test vector fields A,B? Use the unreduced RCD and test classes in the cited theorem.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Giglis-distributional-curvature-characterization-of-Alexandrov-spaces-September-24-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

